<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE SUB-PAGE HEADER — handoff README §7, «Единое лекало».
  ============================================================================

      кнопка назад 44dp (смещена на −10dp влево)
        → крупный заголовок 24sp/700
        → необязательное пояснение 13sp
        → группы карточек

  It is @layout/view_toolbar's replacement ON SUB-SCREENS ONLY, and it is a
  different object rather than a variant of one: view_toolbar draws a 16sp title
  BESIDE the back arrow, which is the shape a tab screen and a form want. §7 puts
  the title UNDER the arrow at 24sp/700, which turns the top of the page into a
  heading the eye lands on before it starts reading rows. Home and the tab screens
  keep view_toolbar; nothing here changes for them.

  THE IDS ARE view_toolbar's ON PURPOSE. ToolbarSlots resolves toolbar_back,
  toolbar_leading_gap, toolbar_title, toolbar_action and toolbar_hairline by id,
  so every screen that already calls ToolbarBinder.bind / attachTo keeps working
  after nothing more than swapping the include's layout= attribute. A screen that
  wants the optional note reaches for @id/toolbar_note itself — that slot is this
  file's own and ships gone.

  THE GUTTER ARITHMETIC, and where the −10dp went. §7 measures a 44dp back control
  pulled 10dp left, which lands its 24dp glyph on the 16dp screen gutter
  (16 − 10 + (44 − 24) / 2 = 16): the shift exists so the GLYPH sits on the gutter
  and not the edge of its touch target. This file reached the same pixel from the
  other side — Widget.Departament.Button.Icon.Toolbar is a 48dp target, the Android
  touch floor that 44 is under, so a 4dp lead-in put the glyph at 4 + 12 = 16.

  EXCEPT IT DID NOT, and no padding was ever going to make it. MaterialButton's
  iconGravity is textStart, so the library centres the glyph in the box and a padding only
  shifts it by half the difference between its two sides; and the box was wrap_content, so
  it measured a line box this control has no text for — 68 × 64, not 48. What places the
  glyph now is an EXACT 48dp box with a symmetric padding (the style's) and a per-slot
  split of the 20dp of inset, which moves the glyph and its press disc together. The full
  arithmetic is in @style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon.Toolbar.

  And the lead-in is GONE, on owner report 0.4.9: «эту кнопку нужно сделать чуть
  левее». The 48dp target is flush with the screen edge — the whole target on screen,
  nothing clipped, and the arrow reads as belonging to the edge of the page rather
  than floating inside it. view_toolbar.xml carries the identical change, so the back
  affordance still does not move between the two headers.

  BOTH SIDES ARE ON 16 NOW, which is §7's лекало and the third time the owner has asked
  for this arrow: «кнопка назад опять съехала, надо ее левее». Its 20dp of inset is split
  6/14 (@dimen/toolbar_back_plate_inset_lead), and an inset split moves the GLYPH and its
  press disc together WITHOUT moving the box — so the ink reaches the gutter, the arrow
  starts on the same line as the 24sp title below it, and the box is still 0…48 against
  the screen edge with every dp of it touchable. The header used to be 4dp asymmetric on
  the argument that those two could not both be had; the argument and its answer are on
  @id/toolbar_back in view_toolbar.xml.

  56 IS A MINIMUM ON THE BAR AND THE TITLE HAS NO HEIGHT AT ALL. At font scale
  200% a 24sp headline needs ~50dp of line box; every text box here is
  wrap_content and grows with it (00-rules.md 14.5).

  THE HAIRLINE ships at alpha 0 and is faded in by ToolbarBinder.attachTo once the
  content behind it has scrolled. It never appears at rest, and nothing else about
  this header changes on scroll — no colour, no elevation, no shadow.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/toolbar"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:background="?android:attr/colorBackground"
    android:elevation="0dp"
    android:orientation="vertical">

    <!-- The back row. §7 «padding:4px 16px 0» — the 4 above the control. There is no
         leading padding any more: the back target starts at the screen edge and it is
         the GLYPH, at 12, that carries the alignment (see the arithmetic above).

         AND NO TRAILING PADDING EITHER, which is the whole of «вот нашел что плюсик
         сверху он левее, надо правее опять сделать». It carried space_4, and that 4 did
         two things nobody had counted. It held the action's ink at 22dp from the screen
         edge while view_toolbar.xml — same binder, same slot, no such padding — held its
         at 18: the header's own two variants disagreed by 4dp about where an action
         goes. And being PADDING on a ViewGroup that clips to it by default, it was also
         a clip line 4dp inside the screen, so the action's box (which is pulled PAST
         the edge to reach the gutter) had its press plate cut on it — the same shear
         the owner photographed on the row's «⋮».

         The distance an action stands off the edge belongs to the binder, per glyph,
         because the two glyphs need different ones. A bar-wide padding cannot express
         that and can only get in the binder's way.

         AND THE 4 THAT IS LEFT DOES NOT CLIP. clipToPadding defaults to true, so every
         padding on a ViewGroup is also a clip line — that is what was shearing the row's
         press disc one component up (see view_row.xml). Nothing is drawn above this bar's
         4dp today, and turning the clip off is what keeps that a fact rather than an
         arithmetic result. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/toolbar_bar"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:baselineAligned="false"
        android:clipToPadding="false"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_4">

        <!-- ICON GAP CLOSED (as in view_toolbar): @drawable/ic_chevron_left is a real
             left-pointing glyph. It used to be ic_chevron_right under
             android:scaleX="-1", and that mirror never survived to the screen —
             @anim/press_icon, which this style carries, has a DEFAULT item animating
             scaleX to 1.0 and it fires on attach, so all 17 sub-pages shipped a back
             arrow pointing right. Do not put a scaleX mirror back; the new drawable is
             android:autoMirrored, which is what RTL wants regardless.

             THE BOX IS AN EXACT 48 AND THE PADDING IS THE STYLE'S — read the twin note in
             view_toolbar.xml. wrap_content measured a line box this control has no text
             for, so it stood 68 wide and 64 tall and dragged the whole bar to 68; the
             press plate inside it was a 48×44 stadium rather than the 28dp disc every
             comment here promises.

             AND THE 6/14 INSET SPLIT IS WHAT PUTS ITS INK ON 16 while the box stays flush
             with the screen edge — the whole of «кнопка назад опять съехала, надо ее
             левее», with the 48dp target intact. @dimen/toolbar_back_plate_inset_lead. -->
        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_back"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon.Toolbar"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:contentDescription="@string/cd_back"
            android:insetLeft="@dimen/toolbar_back_plate_inset_lead"
            android:insetRight="@dimen/toolbar_back_plate_inset_trail"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_chevron_left" />

        <!-- ToolbarBinder shows this when a screen passes no activity, i.e. has no
             back affordance. A sub-page always has one, so it ships gone. -->
        <Space
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_leading_gap"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/space_12"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:visibility="gone" />

        <Space
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="1" />

        <!-- AT MOST ONE, and on §7's lekalo most screens have none: an action is a
             row in a card, where it can carry a name. The slot stays because
             ToolbarBinder resolves it and because «Добавить правило» style toolbar
             actions already bound here must keep working.

             THE INSET SPLIT MOVES THE GLYPH, THE PADDING KEEPS THE PLATE UNDER IT — read
             the identical note in view_toolbar.xml and @dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_lead.
             The 18/12 padding pair that used to be here is what put the disc 3dp off the
             «+» sitting on it, which is the second half of «фон не по центру, неровный
             фон в общем, неправильный». -->
        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_action"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon.Toolbar"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:insetLeft="@dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_lead"
            android:insetRight="@dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_trail"
            android:visibility="gone"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_more_vert_24dp"
            tools:ignore="ContentDescription"
            tools:visibility="visible" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- §7 «крупный заголовок 24sp/700», 8 under the back control. Headline is the
         ramp's 24/700 role; the face is @font/golos_text_bold, which has Cyrillic —
         the wordmark face does not, and that is D-11. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/toolbar_title"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Headline"
        tools:text="Локальный прокси" />

    <!-- §7 «необязательное пояснение 13sp», 6 under the title. One sentence that
         says what the screen is for; a note that restates the title is deleted, not
         written. Ships gone — a screen shows it by giving it text. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/toolbar_note"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_6"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:text="Отсканируйте QR-код, показанный на телевизоре."
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- FLUSH UNDER THE TITLE, with no gap of its own. §6 puts a section header's own
         22dp of padding directly under the page title and the prototype measures zero
         between them; a padding here plus a margin here used to add 17dp to every
         sub-screen before its first word. The hairline still ships at alpha 0. -->
    <View
        android:id="@+id/toolbar_hairline"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/stroke_hairline"
        android:alpha="0"
        android:background="?attr/colorOutlineVariant" />
</LinearLayout>
